  "description": "This flexible Nigerian salad combines crisp vegetables, tangy salad cream, and beans for a refreshing, make-ahead dish that's perfect for any gathering.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: wine → sherry vinegar; Dijon grain mustard → whole grain mustard; shredded white cabbage → green cabbage; shredded romaine lettuce → iceberg lettuce; firm plum → Roma tomatoes; drained canned black-eyed peas → canned vegetarian baked beans\n\nNotes: Store-bough shredded cabbage or coleslaw mix may be substituted for the freshly shredded cabbage.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: The salad cream can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 7 days.\nThe salad can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 3 days.",
